      "Resting proximal pulmonary artery shear is literature-dependent (reported ~0.5-2 Pa); verify the 1.5 Pa target against your specific reference before committing.",
      "1.5 Pa exceeds the HUVEC registry shear range (0.1-1 Pa, microvascular convention); confirm HUVEC tolerates large-artery shear or consider a pulmonary-artery endothelial cell (HPAEC) line.",
      "600 uL/min is a high flow for a single channel — confirm the syringe pump and tubing can sustain it without leakage; pressure drop is only ~300 Pa so this is not limiting.",
